e non-zero terms in the Taylor expansion of $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ about the point $x=2.$\n\n$\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}=${{field-1}}\n$-\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x-2)\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x-2)^{2}-⋯$" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349327 1113 #uuid "5ffe3b19-ff41-5d63-a19d-8b0f648f4bbc" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349327 1145 "We use Taylor's theorem in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ and $a=2.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}={x}^{-2} \\\\ f(2) & ={2}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}=-2{x}^{-3} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =-2(2)^{-3}=-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}=6{x}^{-4} \\\\ {f}^{″}(2) & =6(2)^{-4}=\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{4}+(-\\frac{1}{4})(x-2)+\\frac{(\\frac{3}{8})}{2!}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{4})}{3!}(x-2)^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}(x-2)+\\frac{3}{16}(x-2)^{2}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349328 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349329 13194139535441 true] [17592186349328 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535441 true] [17592186349328 1041 "field-1" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349328 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349329 13194139535441 true] [17592186349328 1110 #uuid "87d877f6-cc92-51aa-b000-1e8f90032716" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349329 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349329 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535441 true] [17592186349329 1111 #uuid "22820e9b-bd84-5f3e-abd7-cef8a3172d72" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349331 13194139535441 true] [17592186349330 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535441 true] [17592186349330 1041 "field-2" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349330 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349331 13194139535441 true] [17592186349330 1110 #uuid "f6703ed6-a312-5b8d-a9ba-9137ef9c355e" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349331 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535441 true] [17592186349331 1111 #uuid "053eedb6-f960-5ac1-a65e-f3e7fa4d8a26" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349333 13194139535441 true] [17592186349332 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535441 true] [17592186349332 1041 "field-3" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349332 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349333 13194139535441 true] [17592186349332 1110 #uuid "e9661ce6-503c-5b08-9ae7-3ca36a929843" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349333 1034 "\\frac{3}{16}" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349333 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535441 true] [17592186349333 1111 #uuid "4115bc0f-5931-5264-865d-c2905db85b2f" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349334 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349335 13194139535441 true] [17592186349334 1089 "q-354043" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349334 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535441 true] [17592186349334 1100 "Use the first two non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ about $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ to approximate the value of $cot\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0.2).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$cot\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0.2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349334 1113 #uuid "4e83ae35-68ee-5980-9c6a-1add762ce26e" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349334 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ and $a=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ f\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =cot\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-{csc}^{2}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =-{csc}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-1+(-2)(x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+⋯ \\\\  & =-1-2(x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0.2$ into the above to approximate $cot\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0.2).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0.2) & ≈-1-2(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0.2-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-1-2(0.2) \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349335 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349336 13194139535441 true] [17592186349335 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535441 true] [17592186349335 1041 "field-1" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349335 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349336 13194139535441 true] [17592186349335 1110 #uuid "7bf922a0-486f-57ea-bc50-3ce1f4895987" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349336 1034 "-1.4" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535441 true] [17592186349336 1111 #uuid "5674f98c-dcd1-5e56-bf7c-123332fdb737" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349337 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349338 13194139535441 true] [17592186349337 1089 "q-83187" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349337 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535441 true] [17592186349337 1100 "Find the first three non-zero terms in the Taylor expansion of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ centered about the point $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349337 1113 #uuid "16609029-055a-5cb8-ad13-f4db9797bcc6" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349337 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $a=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ f(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {f}^{(5)}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(5)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0+(-1)(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{0}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2} \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{3!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}+\\frac{0}{4!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{4}+\\frac{(-1)}{5!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{5}+⋯ \\\\  & =-(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{6}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}-\\frac{1}{120}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{5}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349339 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349340 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349341 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349342 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349343 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1041 "selection" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349341 13194139535441 true] [17592186349338 1110 #uuid "d1beacd1-2256-5a17-8ccd-084c6881cd33" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349339 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{9}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}-\\frac{1}{27}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{5}+⋯" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535441 true] [17592186349339 1111 #uuid "74146c92-49ee-51db-963a-8f1483f0f15b" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349340 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{12}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}-\\frac{1}{240}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{5}+⋯" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349340 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535441 true] [17592186349340 1111 #uuid "250ceca8-2e7d-5403-bafb-76dc688f0cca" 13194139535441 true] [17592186349341 1034 "\\operatorname{c